# To investigate or fix
- Steering or adding in prompts mid turn ( inbetween tool calls ) seems to not work as intended, and only send after the agent finishes all of its tool calls? Steering MUST directly inject in 'mid-turn' - which is basically right after the current LLM response comes in. This means going in before any other action after the current action/response from the endpoint comes in.
- After the recent mouse scrolling update, selecting lines for copy pasting doesn't work consistently anymore.
- Auto-compact doesn't seem to work properly- the notice triggers, but the conversation history sent to the LLM endpoint seems to invalidate the entire cache? Is it because it's modified from the system prompt? Should it be tied to a 'user message` but sent by the system instead?
- When LLM intends to run a inline python tool call - it can grow to really long tool approval prompt. Cant scroll properly to view the entire thing. (PgUp/PgDown works during approval, but prompt content itself still not scrollable)
  - Related point: When multiple messages are then queued - they fire off in turns and not altogether as one message. this causes issues. Might need a way to handle/edit/delete queued messages.


# To Test
- Windows - When pasting multiple lines ( e.g copied from notepad, multiple commands ) - it seems to send the first line only ( might be due to breaklines or something? ) instead of the whole chunk. While default terminal behaves that way, gohome is a coding assistant so pasting long chunks of text should be the norm, and send only when pressing enter is the behaviour to match.
- Drastic slowdown on rendering when large thinking or replies after 40k context? (render throttle added, but underlying issue may persist)
- sudo password input testing
- Auto-scrolling: When user manually scrolls up or down, the UI stops tracking the latest messages and doesn't auto scroll anymore. This is intended when the user is moving either through scrolling or pressing up/down or pgup/pgdn . BUT if the user has scrolled to the bottom, the auto-scroll should then be enabled to track the new turns/LLM outputs. 
